.TH RBA 1 "2026-11-23" "rba 0.1.0" "Remote Biometric Authenticator"
.SH NAME
rba \- Remote Biometric Authenticator controller
.SH SYNOPSIS
rba [\-\-socket PATH] <COMMAND> [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBrba\fP is the command-line client for the Remote Biometric Authenticator system.
It is designed to be ADB-like: many commands start the daemon automatically
if it is not already running, and the binary is self-contained (no separate
installer scripts, no secrets in argv).
.SH COMMANDS
The following subcommands are available:
.TP
\fBstart-server\fP
Start a user-level \fbrbad\fP daemon in the background. If a system-level
daemon is installed, this is a no-op (use \fIsystemctl start rbad\fP instead).
.TP
\fBkill-server\fP
Stop the user-level \fbrbad\fP daemon started by \fBstart-server\fP. If a
system-level daemon is managed by systemd, this is a no-op (use
\fIsystemctl stop rbad\fP instead).
.TP
\fBdevices\fP
Show paired authenticators with their device ID, state, users, root access
status, and link state.
.TP
\fBstatus\fP
Show daemon status: host information, paired device count, and enabled
integrations (gdm, polkit, sudo).
.TP
\fBpair\fP
Pair a new biometric authenticator. Waits for the device to confirm, then
prints \fIPaired.\fP (or \fIPaired \fRmodel\fP when \fB--device\fP is set).
.TP
\fBauth \-[u]ser USER\fP
Authenticate the specified Linux user using a paired authenticator.
.TP
\fBunpair \-\-device D\fP
Remove trust for a device. Owner or root may invoke this.
.TP
\fBrevoke \-\-device D\fP
Revoke an authenticator immediately. Root only.
.TP
\fBenable \fRbackend\fP
Enable a host integration (gdm, polkit, sudo) on Linux. Requires root.
.TP
\fBdisable \fRbackend\fP
Roll back a host integration on Linux. Requires root.
.TP
\fBversion\fP
Print the product and protocol version.
.TP
\fBhelp\fP
Show this help message and exit 0.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB--socket PATH\fP
Control socket path. Defaults to the system socket if installed, otherwise a
per-user socket under \fB$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/rba\fP.
.TP
\fB\-s USER \|\-\-user USER\fP
Linux user to authenticate (defaults to \fB$USER\fP).
.TP
\fB\-d DEVICE \|\-\-device DEVICE\fP
Device identifier (HOST:PORT or device ID) to target for unpair/revoke.
.TP
\fB\-\-code-entry \{device|host\}\fP
Pairing code entry mode: \fBdevice\fP (host shows code, device types it) or
\fBhost\fP (device shows code, terminal prompts).
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout MS\fP
Authentication timeout in milliseconds (default 90000).
.TP
\fB\-\-state-dir PATH\fP
User-level state directory (default \fB$XDG_STATE_HOME/rba\fP, or
\fB$HOME/.local/state/rba\fP, or \fB/tmp/rba-state-\fRuid\fP).
.TP
\fB\-\-audit-log PATH\fP
Audit log path (default under the state directory).
.TP
\fB\-\-bind ADDR\fP
Bind address for the daemon (IP:PORT).
.TP
\fB\-\-port N\fP
TCP port for the daemon (default 47123).
.TP
\fB\-\-no-mdns\fP
Disable mDNS advertisement.
.TP
\fB\-\-mdns-interface NAME\fP
Specify which interface mDNS should use.
.TP
\fB\-\-host-name NAME\fP
Host name shown on the device.
.TP
\fB\-\-foreground\fP
Run the daemon in the foreground (for \fBstart-server\fP).
.TP
\fB\-\-socket-explicit\fP
Use the explicitly given socket path without falling back to system default.
.TP
\fB\-\-state-dir\fP PATH
See \fB--state-dir\fP.
.TP
\fB\-\-audit-log\fP PATH
See \fB--audit-log\fP.
.TP
\fB\-\-bind\fP ADDR
See \fB--bind\fP.
.TP
\fB\-\-port\fP N
See \fB--port\fP.
.TP
\fB\-\-no-mdns\fP
See \fB--no-mdns\fP.
.TP
\fB\-\-mdns-interface\fP NAME
See \fB--mdns-interface\fP.
.TP
\fB\-\-host-name\fp NAME
See \fB--host-name\fP.
.TP
\fB\-\-foreground\fP
See \fB--foreground\fP.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBRBA_SOCKET\fP
Control socket (overrides the default choice).
.TP
\fBRBA_STATE_DIR\fP
User-level state directory.
.TP
\fBRBA_RUNTIME_DIR\fP
User-level runtime directory (default \fB$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/rba\fP).
.SH EXIT STATUS
The following exit codes are used:
.TP
\fB0\fP
Success.
.TP
\fB1\fP
Error (usage, connection refused, pairing timeout, permission denied).
.TP
\fB2\fP
Unknown command or invalid arguments.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fB/usr/local/bin/rba\fP
User-facing binary (installed by \fImake release\fP or \fIinstall-local.sh\fP).
.TP
\fB/usr/libexec/rbad\fP
Daemon binary (installed by \fImake release\fP or \fIinstall-local.sh\fP).
.TP
\fB/usr/lib/security/pam_rba.so\fP
PAM module (installed by \fImake release\fP or \fIinstall-local.sh\fP).
.TP
\fB/etc/systemd/system/rbad.service\fP
Systemd service file (used by system install).
.TP
\fB/var/lib/rba\fP
Default state directory (root-only).
.TP
\fB/var/log/rba\fP
Default audit log directory (root-only).
.TP
\fB$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/rba/control.sock\fP
Per-user control socket (when no system install).
.SH SEE ALSO
rbad(8), pam_rba(8), systemctl(8), adc(1)
.SH BUGS
Windows support remains feasibility-only; the Windows Hello Companion Device
Framework is deprecated.
.SH AUTHOR
Written by burtvadr for the Remote Biometric Authenticator project.